{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_residue_monodromy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_residue_monodromy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Complex"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_residue_monodromy_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_residue_monodromy_phase","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L112-L122","doc":"**CONJECTURE.** The exact Picard-Lefschetz monodromy phase around the\nsingular fibre $\\zeta_5$ on the homology of the hyperelliptic quintic $\\mathcal{X}_5$\nevaluates to the $1/\\sqrt{5}$ chiral residue and the $+2.1^\\circ$ H₂S angle.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5_abs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5_abs","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L107-L110","doc":"Final Step: The absolute value of the algebraically real Gauss sum is $\\sqrt{5}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5_eval","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L99-L105","doc":"Step 6: Combine steps 3, 4, and 5 to prove the Gauss sum is exactly $\\sqrt{5}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.cos_two_pi_fifths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.cos_two_pi_fifths","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L88-L97","doc":"Step 5: The exact trigonometric value of $\\cos(2\\pi/5)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_add_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_add_inv","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L65-L86","doc":"Step 4: The sum of the roots $\\zeta_5 + \\zeta_5^4$ evaluates to $2 \\cos(2\\pi/5)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5_reduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5_reduced","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L59-L63","doc":"Step 3: The Gauss sum reduces algebraically to $1 + 2\\zeta_5 + 2\\zeta_5^4$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_reductions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_reductions","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L52-L57","doc":"Step 2: Reduce the higher powers modulo 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_pow_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.zeta5_pow_five","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L45-L50","doc":"Step 1: Prove that $\\zeta_5$ is a 5th root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.gauss_sum_5","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L41-L43","doc":"The exact quadratic Gauss sum over $\\mathbb{Z}_5$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.Zeta5MonodromyContext.claim_monodromy_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.Zeta5MonodromyContext.claim_monodromy_phase","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Manuscript identity: The integral is mathematically proportional to the Gauss sum, and its phase yields the +2.1° bond angle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.Zeta5MonodromyContext.DeltaTheta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.Zeta5MonodromyContext.DeltaTheta","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQuintic/zeta5_residue_monodromy.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The H₂S residual phase angle (+2.1°). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.Zeta5MonodromyContext.residue_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HyperellipticQuintic.Zeta5MonodromyContext.residue_eval","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HyperellipticQui